"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-09T12:32:50Z","updated_at":"2026-06-09T12:32:50Z","body":"Seems that plugin might be the issue then, the specific decision to error when doing these operations are done, but as you say it doesn't affect behavior (except in some cases where it fixes deeper errors), it might be worth documenting in the respective methods that it errors as well as returning a safe value","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4659735506/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4745474407","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120107#issuecomment-4745474407","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120107","id":4745474407,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABGtoxZw","user":{"login":"aidandavey","id":71520018,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNTIwMDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71520018?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidandavey","html_url":"https://github.com/aidandavey","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidandavey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidandavey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidandavey/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidandavey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidandavey/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidandavey/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidandavey/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidandavey/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidandavey/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-18T19:32:16Z","updated_at":"2026-06-18T19:59:43Z","body":"[Heightmap_holes_warning_spam_4-7.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/29110049/Heightmap_holes_warning_spam_4-7.zip)\n\nThis is still an issue I think - using NAN values in a heightmap to signify a hole causes the GodotPhysics system to spam the warning while move_and_slide() ing\n\nIt can be seen in the Terrain3D demo project by painting some holes and moving the player towards them.\n\nI also manually built a heightmap shape with NAN holes and confirmed it can be replicated without the plugin - see uploaded MRP\n\nJolt seems to not have the same issue. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4745474407/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4752929908","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120107#issuecomment-4752929908","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120107","id":4752929908,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABG0v0dA","user":{"login":"tldmbruno","id":118130235,"node_id":"U_kgDOBwqGOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118130235?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno","html_url":"https://github.com/tldmbruno","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-19T15:40:01Z","updated_at":"2026-06-19T15:40:01Z","body":"For my case, it was caused right after I upgraded to Godot 4.7. When the Terrain3D had any holes in it, while I was using GodotPhysics instead of JOLT. Switched to Jolt and now the issue is fixed.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4752929908/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4753468597","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120107#issuecomment-4753468597","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120107","id":4753468597,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABG1QstQ","user":{"login":"TokisanGames","id":632766,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzMjc2Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/632766?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames","html_url":"https://github.com/TokisanGames","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-19T17:04:12Z","updated_at":"2026-06-19T18:04:13Z","body":"```\nWARNING: Vector3 cannot be normalized, the elements must be finite. Making (0, 0, 0) as a fallback.\n     at: normalize (./core/math/vector3.h:551)\n```\nThis is a regression in Godot Physics or Vector3 introduced in 4.7dev3. It is not present in 4.6.3, 4.7dev1, 4.7dev2. It is not a documentation or a plugin issue. In our case it's triggered by NANs in the vertices of a HeightmapShape to punch holes in the collision. It affects move_and_slide() and raycasts.\n\nQuick test: Download Terrain3D from the asset lib, turn right 90 degrees, fly towards the mountain and into the cave.\n\nedit:\nMost likely caused by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116427\nThis adds a warning which causes the error spam and kills engine performance.\nEither Godot Physics should not try to normalize nans, or Vector3 should not dump spam onto the console.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4753468597/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4753904917","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120107#issuecomment-4753904917","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120107","id":4753904917,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABG1rVFQ","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-19T18:29:10Z","updated_at":"2026-06-19T18:29:10Z","body":"Since attempting to normalize NaN is completely incorrect code, we should fix the code that is normalizing NaN, rather than the Vector3 side. Is there specific code in GodotPhysics that does this? I’m not sure if GodotPhysics is still being maintained, but adding an `is_finite()` check there would be a step in the right direction.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4753904917/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4775579878","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120107#issuecomment-4775579878","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120107","id":4775579878,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHKWQ5g","user":{"login":"jonathan-durbin","id":31511197,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNTExMTk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31511197?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathan-durbin","html_url":"https://github.com/jonathan-durbin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathan-durbin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathan-durbin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathan-durbin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathan-durbin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathan-durbin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathan-durbin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathan-durbin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathan-durbin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathan-durbin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-23T04:26:02Z","updated_at":"2026-06-23T04:26:02Z","body":"Wanted to add a MRP to this. I encountered this warning only for my (very light) custom 3D Gizmo (nowhere else in my main project), so I included that script. I get 162 warnings in the debugger pane upon running the node_3d scene in the linked project below.\n\n[vector-3-math-error-testing.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/29233338/vector-3-math-error-testing.zip)\n\nIf I add a small offset (0.0001) to the incoming (zero) vector, the warnings go away. My confusion was coming from the fact that selecting one of the warnings seemed to lead me to the wrong line in my script.\n\nHopefully this will be useful to a future developer!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4775579878/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4779407688","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120107#issuecomment-4779407688","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120107","id":4779407688,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHN_5SA","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-23T12:55:18Z","updated_at":"2026-06-23T16:26:37Z","body":"> My confusion was coming from the fact that selecting one of the warnings seemed to lead me to the wrong line in my script.\n\n@jonathan-durbin The error line is correct. Although an error occurred internally in the setter of the `height` property in the `PrimitiveMesh` class in the C++ code, the line number displayed in GDScript is correct. If we were to improve this, we would probably need to add a guard within the `PrimitiveMesh` class.\n\n_Edited:_\nI sent https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120582 to fix that issue.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4779407688/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]